    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.operators\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nI have this mapping in my configs:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set({\"n\", \"x\", \"o\"}, \"_\", \"H\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd narrowed that down to why my mini.operators `grr`, `gmm`, `gxx` and possibly `g==` aren't working as intended. (Note, `gss` works)\r\n\r\nWhatever I've mapped to `_` acts as the motion, so in my case, would operate til the top of the visible window.\r\n\r\nI'm wondering, is there like some `!` (bang) missing somewhere in the code where re-mappings should be ignored? Or some similar small thing like this.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nv0.10.1\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n#### Minimal config\r\n\r\n`minimal.lua`:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"o\", \"_\", \"<cmd>echo('Hi!!!')<cr>\")\r\n\r\nvim.fn.system({\r\n    \"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth=1\",\r\n    \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.operators\",\r\n    \"plugins/mini.operators\"\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:append(\"plugins/mini.operators\")\r\nrequire(\"mini.operators\").setup()\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Repro\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ echo \"test foo bar\" > test.xt\r\n$ nvim -nu minimal.lua test.txt\r\n```\r\n\r\nPress `gmm`\r\n\r\nNotice how only the character under cursor gets duplicated, and the custom keymapping `<cmd>echo('Hi!!!')<cr>` is used.\r\n\r\nSimilar thing happens with `gxx`, `grr` and `g==`, but **not** `gss`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nI expect that I can have an operator-pending mapping on `_` without affecting the behavior of this plugin.",
