            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Referenced above I have a fix using `feedkeys` with the `\"n\"` flag (\"do not remap keys\") that allows me to create prefixes cleanly without workarounds :)\n> \n> Let me know if that's of interest, or if the stance is still \"not planned\", please ignore\n\nSorry, this is still a workaround, just in the 'mini.operators' code. I'd rather not use three `nvim_feedkeys` calls to remedy a use case which I (somewhat strongly) think is a bad idea to begin with. The usage of `_` is [documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e554890210cd29d017d6a0c1b1a46f995dcf9e64/doc/mini-operators.txt#L396-L398) while if user wants to override built-in textobject, they should be aware of the consequences. So I am afraid this is still not planned.\n\nBut anyway thanks for the suggestion and enthusiasm for custom workarounds!\n\n---\n\nWhile at it, I also don't think it is a good idea to allow `<C-c>` to be remappable. Although there is now precedence in 'mini.snippets', that is for Insert mode mapping. Other instances of its usages are not remappable and I think it is a good thing.",
